        {
          "id": "SP_SINOFLUSTRA_AMOYENSIS",
          "name": "Sinoflustra amoyensis",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Sinoflustra",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Colony encrusting, multiserial, unilamellar. Ancestrula and early astogeny not observed. Autozooids subrectangular, rounded distally, slender, typically twice as long as wide, 0.43 – 0.63 mm long by 0.18 – 0.28 mm wide; zooidal boundaries marked by a narrow fissure; opesia occupying two-thirds of frontal surface, elongate inverted pear-shaped; cryptocyst convex, widest proximally, narrowing distally, covered by small pustules, about 10 – 16 cryptocystal spinules extending from mural rim over proximal two-thirds of opesia, but not meeting, distal third of opesia broad and spineless (Fig. 5 F); gymnocyst lacking. Spines present at distolateral corners of autozooids, spines broken off in studied specimens, leaving a small rounded triangular base with a central pore (Fig. 5 F). Avicularia not observed.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:1006523",
          "uuid": "e77f0ffa-0351-51e-945-f64d0d47b20a20",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "6Z38Y"
            ],
            "checklistbank": "be40e3e0-bb34-41b7-b959-fffd2296da9d"
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:6Z38Y",
          "authorship": "Robertson",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_SINOFLUSTRA_ANNAE",
          "name": "Sinoflustra annae",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Bryozoan",
          "lineage": "Sinoflustra",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Colony encrusting, unilaminar, uniserial to multiserial, fragile. Autozooids rectangular, longer than wide (LZ 446 – 589 µm [498 ± 52, N = 20]; WZ 195 – 341 µm [264 ± 44, N = 20]), autozooidal margin indistinct (Fig. 8 A). Cryptocyst well developed proximally, granular, wide, becoming narrower in some zooids. Opesia subrectangular to ovoidal (LOp 379 – 487 µm [426 ± 31, N = 20]; WOp 147 – 290 µm [211 ± 49, N = 20]), occupying two-thirds of autozooidal length, surrounded by a spinous cryptocyst; opesia more circular and broader just before the bifurcation; rim raised, crenulated, with 10 – 12 slender spines occupying almost entirely its proximal and lateral regions. Operculum distal, straight to slightly curved, well developed. Avicularia vicarious, spatulate, longer than wide (LAv 650 – 696 µm [677 ± 23, N = 2]; WAv 195 – 248 µm [221 ± 26, N = 2]), almost twice the size of an autozooid; cryptocyst granular, narrow, wider proximally (Fig. 8 C). A row of uniporous mural septula on distal (Fig. 8 B) and lateral transverse walls (Fig. 8 D). Kenozooids absent.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:1006525",
